 {
  "schema": 1,
  "kind": "keys-density",
  "id": "track-mood",
  "revision": 1,
  "name": "Mood, over a whole track",
  "scope": "track",
  "says": "The lab's mood over a real form: the keys land on section lines and in the exposed, drum-free passages most, a drop once at its line and a long full passage once more at most; the first landing after the mixing intro's clean bars, none in the outro's last bars, and a budget for the whole track.",
  "note": "A whole track's row (the app's three, `scope: track`; the lab's Arc reads the other three). `classes` maps a section's kind to its rule (`otherwise` for a kind the row does not name, so a form row's new kind lands somewhere); each rule's `ways` are drawn per section off a stream of its own, `from` the first landing (a bar of the section, or \"half\"), `every` the gaps after it as [bars, weight]. A landing in the first `cleanBars` of the track or its last `cleanEndBars` is not played (the mixing regions), nor one nearer than `minGapBars` to the one before. `budget.most` is the most landings a track has: past it, the class last in `keep` loses its landings first, a section's later ones before its line, the latest first. A rule's `levelDb`, `send` and `dry` are the keys low and very wet under a full section, as the lab's drops. `bed`: the bed around a landing, its `voices`, how far before a bare landing's strike its moving voice leaves (`bareLeadSteps`), how long after the strike it comes back (`returnSteps`), and the release it leaves on (`thinRelease`, seconds).",
  "cleanBars": 16,
  "cleanEndBars": 16,
  "minGapBars": 4,
  "budget": {
   "most": 12,
   "keep": [
    "exposed",
    "intro",
    "outro",
    "line",
    "build",
    "inside"
   ]
  },
